From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carlos Fundora <carlosfundora@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 10:07:13 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Relax Q-MATH Rayon guard; keep Rayon an optional kernel
 dependency

Remove the btc-mining compile_error! guard from rayon and rayon-core and
drop the btc-mining marker features. The guard blocked every consumer that
reaches Rayon transitively, including the embedded SurrealDB benchmark
persistence stack (surrealdb-core -> diskann-utils / ext-sort / geo-types).
A single feature set also stops rayon-core rebuilding when builds alternate
between guarded and unguarded selections. Optionality is enforced at the
consumer: Q-MATH's only direct dependency is runtime_zen2's optional rayon.

Record the fork, branch layout and fetch-only upstream update procedure in
QMATH_VENDOR_PROVENANCE.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
